---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { buildDemoArticles } from "../modules/CB-M11/demo-articles.mjs";
import { buildDemoMarketReadiness } from "../modules/CB-M11/demo-market-readiness.mjs";
import inspectorCssUrl from "./developers-inspector.css?url&no-inline";

export const prerender = false;
const articleExample = buildDemoArticles();
const marketExample = buildDemoMarketReadiness();
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Developer sandbox · CoinBlink DEMO"
  description="Offline synthetic developer API demonstration plus content-free live status and publisher catalog endpoints. No real articles, accounts, licensing, billing or market data."
>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href={inspectorCssUrl} />
  <main id="main" class="not-found">
    <p class="eyebrow">M11 · DEMO ONLY · NOT PUBLISHED</p>
    <h1>Developer sandbox</h1>
    <p class="body-copy">
      Explore a deliberately limited JSON response made from three invented educational
      examples. These records are not news, are not published, and are not licensed
      for commercial redistribution.
    </p>
    <p class="body-copy">
      There is no self-serve signup. Partner keys are issued by the owner, and the
      metered endpoint below requires one; the sandbox endpoints stay open and
      synthetic. No market prices, private drafts or payments are connected.
    </p>
    <p class="body-copy">
      No live quotes, trading or licensed market redistribution. The blocked market
      readiness demo shows why BTC, ETH and SOL are not publicly usable.
    </p>
    <nav aria-label="Developer demonstration">
      <a class="button button--primary" href="/v1/demo/articles">Open synthetic JSON</a>
      <a href="/v1/demo/market-readiness">Open synthetic market readiness JSON</a>
      <a href="/en/news">Read fictional news examples (EN)</a>
      <a href="/en">Return to demo home</a>
    </nav>
    <section aria-labelledby="m11-example">
      <h2 id="m11-example">Local request example</h2>
      <pre><code>GET /v1/demo/articles

200 OK
Content-Type: application/json
mode: SYNTHETIC
status: DEMO_ONLY
redistributable: false
published: false (every record)
max items: 3

Query parameters: unsupported
Write methods: unsupported
Not the commercial /v1/articles
API.</code></pre>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="m11-metered">
      <h2 id="m11-metered">Metered partner access (API key)</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        <code>GET /v1/status</code> serves the same content-free collection state to a
        registered partner and counts every accepted call against the key plan. Send the key
        as <code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;key&gt;</code> or <code>x-api-key: &lt;key&gt;</code>.
        Keys are issued by the owner and shown once; CoinBlink stores only a digest.
      </p>
      <pre class="m11-status-example"><code>{`GET /v1/status
Authorization: Bearer cbk_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx.&lt;secret&gt;

200 OK
Content-Type: application/json
Cache-Control: no-store

{
  "status": "ok",
  "contract": {
    "version": "v1",
    "license": "CoinBlink operational metadata; no third-party article content",
    "redistribution": false,
    "attribution": { "required": true, "path": "/en/news/sources" }
  },
  "plan": "sandbox",
  "quota": { "limit": 1000, "used": 1, "remaining": 999, "period": "2026-10" },
  "generatedAt": "2026-10-31T12:00:00.000Z",
  "collection": { "status": "ok", "feedsRead": 5, "items": 60 }
}`}</code></pre>
      <p class="body-copy">
        Plans are Sandbox (1&nbsp;000 calls per UTC month, no subscription needed),
        Starter (25&nbsp;000) and Pro (250&nbsp;000); the paid plans require an entitling
        subscription. The counter is atomic, so two concurrent calls cannot pass the limit.
      </p>
      <ul class="body-copy">
        <li><code>401 API_KEY_REQUIRED</code> / <code>401 INVALID_API_KEY</code> — send a valid key.</li>
        <li><code>403 API_KEY_REVOKED</code> — the key was revoked; ask the owner for a new one.</li>
        <li><code>429 QUOTA_EXCEEDED</code> — the plan limit is spent. Honour <code>Retry-After</code>, which counts the seconds to the first instant of the next UTC month.</li>
        <li><code>503 NOT_CONFIGURED</code> — the database binding is missing; retry later.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="body-copy">
        Responses are <code>cache-control: no-store</code> because they are metered per key.
        The payload never contains third-party article text and states
        <code>redistribution: false</code>: attribution to
        <a href="/en/news/sources">the source directory</a> is required.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="m11-news-status">
      <h2 id="m11-news-status">Live collection status (content-free)</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        <code>GET /v1/news/status</code> reports which public RSS feeds responded, how many
        headlines each contributed, the collection time and the rights status. It contains no
        headline text, excerpt, article body or publisher name, so it can be polled from a
        script without redistributing anyone&rsquo;s reporting.
      </p>
      <pre class="m11-status-example"><code>{`GET /v1/news/status

200 OK
Content-Type: application/json
Cache-Control: max-age=60
Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *

{
  "status": "ok",
  "mode": "LIVE_THIRD_PARTY",
  "feedsRead": 5,
  "feedsTotal": 5,
  "items": 60,
  ...
}`}</code></pre>
      <nav aria-label="Live collection status"><a href="/v1/news/status">Open the status JSON</a></nav>
      <p class="body-copy">
        When the reader is disabled the endpoint answers with status <code>disabled</code> and
        an empty feed list. Only GET, HEAD and OPTIONS are supported; query parameters are
        rejected with 400.
      </p>
      <p class="body-copy">
        All three real endpoints return an <code>ETag</code>. Send it back as
        <code>If-None-Match</code> to receive 304 without a body.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="m11-coverage-status">
      <h2 id="m11-coverage-status">Coverage counts (content-free)</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        <code>GET /v1/news/coverage</code> counts the stories carried by more than one
        publisher and how many covered stories name each publisher. It uses the same
        mechanical title matching as the reader and returns aggregates only: no
        headlines, links or article timestamps.
      </p>
      <pre class="m11-status-example"><code>{`GET /v1/news/coverage

200 OK
Content-Type: application/json
Cache-Control: public, max-age=60

{
  "status": "ok",
  "mode": "LIVE_THIRD_PARTY",
  "stories": 4,
  "headlines": 60,
  "rights": "ATTRIBUTION_ONLY",
  "publishers": [{ "id": "coindesk", "stories": 3 }, ...],
  "disclaimer": "Counts only. ..."
}`}</code></pre>
      <nav aria-label="Coverage counts"><a href="/v1/news/coverage">Open the coverage JSON</a></nav>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="m11-source-catalog">
      <h2 id="m11-source-catalog">Publisher catalog (real, metadata only)</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        <code>GET /v1/sources</code> lists the five publishers CoinBlink is allowed to read:
        id, name, home page, RSS feed and the localized reader page for each. It contains no
        headlines, excerpts or article content.
      </p>
      <pre class="m11-status-example"><code>{`GET /v1/sources

200 OK
Content-Type: application/json
Cache-Control: max-age=3600

{
  "status": "ok",
  "count": 5,
  "sources": [
    {
      "id": "coindesk",
      "name": "CoinDesk",
      "home": "https://www.coindesk.com",
      "feed": "https://www.coindesk.com/arc/outboundfeeds/rss",
      "pages": { "en": "/en/news/source/coindesk", ... },
      "rights": "ATTRIBUTION_ONLY"
    },
    ...
  ]
}`}</code></pre>
      <p class="body-copy">Supports the same ETag/304 behaviour as the status endpoint.</p>
      <nav aria-label="Publisher catalog"><a href="/v1/sources">Open the source catalog JSON</a></nav>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="m11-openapi">
      <h2 id="m11-openapi">OpenAPI 3.1 contract</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        The three real endpoints are described in a machine-readable document, including the
        200/304/400/405/503 responses and the content-free schemas. It also supports
        <code>If-None-Match</code>.
      </p>
      <nav aria-label="OpenAPI contract"><a href="/v1/openapi.json">Open the OpenAPI document</a></nav>
    </section>
    <section class="m11-inspector-section" aria-labelledby="m11-inspector-title">
      <h2 id="m11-inspector-title">Inspect synthetic API responses</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        Expand these bounded examples directly in the documentation. They use the
        same fictional models as the GET-only demo endpoints. No request, account,
        license, real market quote, or email is created by expanding a preview.
      </p>
      <details class="m11-inspector" data-m11-example="articles">
        <summary>Show fictional articles JSON</summary>
        <pre><code>{JSON.stringify(articleExample, null, 2)}</code></pre>
      </details>
      <details class="m11-inspector" data-m11-example="market-readiness">
        <summary>Show synthetic blocked-market JSON</summary>
        <pre><code>{JSON.stringify(marketExample, null, 2)}</code></pre>
      </details>
      <p class="body-copy">
        Both examples are unlicensed, unpublished, not redistributable and never LIVE.
        They are not an authorization to publish or redistribute any source.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

